		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Satellite pass times off by 1 hour...]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5027&amp;p=36567#p36567"><![CDATA[
I found the problem with both my TYT with Opengd77 and my AnyTone HT. I<br>had to go into the menus and change the Timezone offset from -5:00hrs to<br>-4:00hrs. When I did that... I had to change the radio's time again by 1<br>hour (wouldn't of had to do this id I didn't originally change the time by<br>1 hour)... and the satellite pass times were correct.<br><br>Now... I'll have to remember this in November when we set our clocks back<br>1 hour. I sure wish they would put an end to this stupid changing the clocks<br>1 hour twice a year.<br><br>Mike - N1EVH<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6514">n1evh</a> — Tue Apr 01, 2025 11:13 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
